      "writtenOn": "2023-02-14T09:48:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "not related to this cl: I noticed that this function calls `BccHandoverMainFlow`. As it takes the bcc handover CBOR bundle and [parses](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:external/open-dice/src/android/bcc.c;l\u003d211;drc\u003d9b25969d7bf3e31c5b7fec5b34c37a304b6a7fa7) it to produce the next bcc handover, I wonder if we really need to call [BccHandover::new](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Virtualization/libs/dice/src/bcc.rs;l\u003d54;drc\u003d54511fda223b4a1eefa5553870d8cb6ae92597c6) to parse the bcc handover before reaching here. The parsed CDIs from the previous boot stage are not used anywhere. \n\nSo, can we remove `BccHandover::new`, just pass the raw bcc handover to main() and call BccHandoverMainFlow on it directly here?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 103,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 103,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "7e03dccc90d29ed0a43bbe270e9f6d8c5a1106d4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
